# onrecord — Cursor rules

Before any task, read these. They are authoritative and they override anything in this file:

- `PROJECT_STATE.md` — scope, principles, validated decisions, **rejected ideas**
- `CLAUDE.md` — the engineering invariants, which apply to every change whether or not they are restated
- `docs/AGENT_ROLES.md` — who does what

## Your role here is editor, not builder

Numbered packets (`OR-###`) belong to Claude Code. You handle sweeps, hand edits, and questions.

**Before starting anything, check for an open packet branch.** If one exists and is unmerged, stop and say so. Only one agent works at a time.

## Do

- Copy and content sweeps
- Read and explain diffs and existing code
- One-line fixes, typos, dead logging
- Harvest a component from `reference/v0-export/` into `src/` **only when a packet asks for it**, rewritten against the real schema
- Run `pnpm verify` before reporting done

## Never

- Change the schema, `src/config/ca-tax.ts`, `PROJECT_STATE.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, or `BUILD_PLAN.md`
- Add a dependency
- Edit anything under `reference/` — it is read-only design reference, never imported from
- Resurrect anything in the Rejected Ideas table in `PROJECT_STATE.md`
- Refactor files unrelated to what was asked
- Take on work that needs an architectural decision — that is a packet. Stop and say so.

## The invariants, in short

Full list in `CLAUDE.md`. The ones a copy sweep is most likely to break:

- Marketing and help copy may not claim behavior the code doesn't have
- No home value estimate, range, or "your home may be worth"
- No loan payoff balance — the record shows the original deed of trust and whether a reconveyance was filed, nothing more
- Never assert Prop 19 eligibility to a consumer; state facts and let them self-identify
- Statutory numbers live only in `src/config/ca-tax.ts`
- No file over 300 lines

## Plain language

The buyer is a working real estate agent, median age 57, who already pays for software they don't open. Short sentences, everyday words, one idea each. If a word makes someone pause for half a second, replace it.

**The distinction that matters:** jargon inside a picture of a document is evidence — the recorder stamp reading `Instrument / Grant Deed / Consideration` stays exactly as it is. Jargon in a sentence that explains something is a lost reader — "a full reconveyance was recorded" becomes "his mortgage was paid off or refinanced."

Banned in explanatory copy: reconveyed, reconveyance, recorded transfers, grant deed, assessed value, base year, parcel, portability, attribution, deed prices, title officer, tax cap.

Keep, because they are the whole point: recorded, the county, the record, actually sold, the real number.

## Report when done

```
SWEEP_REPORT
What: <one line>
Files: <list>
Verify: PASS | FAIL
Notes: <anything the Director should know, or "none">
Commit: <hash>
```

Nothing before it, nothing after it.
